<title>MALAYSIA: Berjaya Industrial requests suspension.</title>
<headline>Berjaya Industrial requests suspension.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berjaya Industrial Bhd said it has requested a suspension in its stock effective from Tuesday pending an announcement.</p>
<p>The company, whose businesses include property development and running hotels, made the request in a statement sent late on Monday to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange. No details were provided, and company officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>In a separate announcement, affiliate company Berjaya Capital Bhd said it is still in the process of finalising negotiations on a proposed transaction, which it did not detail. Its stock closed at 2.40 ringgit on November 15.</p>
<p>Berjaya Capital's businesses include general insurance, securities dealing and trading and future broking.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 230 8911)</p>
</text>
